From: Michael-CY Lee <michael-cy.lee@mediatek.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Oct 2024 08:37:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: answer a TID-to-link mapping negotiation

An AP MLD neither subscribes to the TID-To-Link Mapping Request and
Teardown frames of a non-AP MLD nor handles them in
ieee802_11_rx_protected_eht_action(), so a station gets no Response
frame, and the mapping that it asks for never reaches the driver.

Answer a request where the driver applies a negotiated mapping and its
MLD capabilities declare TID-To-Link Mapping Negotiation Support.
Accept a mapping of both directions with a map for every TID onto the
links that the station set up; deny it with status 133 otherwise. With
support value 1, all TIDs have to map to the same link set
(IEEE Std 802.11be-2024, 35.3.7.2.3). Set the accepted mapping in the
driver once the Response frame is acknowledged, since the negotiation
succeeds only then. A Response frame that is not acknowledged, or a
mapping that the driver refuses, ends in a teardown, so that both MLDs
use the default mapping. Send the Response frame on the link of the
request, on which the station is awake, like the Link Reconfiguration
Response frame, and the Teardown frame after it on the same link. A
Teardown frame of the station sets the
default mapping again, and so does a new association. A Teardown frame
holds the Category and Action fields alone, so accept an Action frame of
that length.

An advertised mapping disables the links outside it for all TIDs
(35.3.7.2.4). Deny a request that maps a TID to such a link while an
advertised mapping is requested or established, and tear down the
negotiated mappings that use such a link when an advertised mapping is
requested.

Only the links that the station set up with success count as its
links, so that no mapping names a refused link. A move of the
association of a non-AP MLD to another link STA moves the negotiated
mapping as well.

Signed-off-by: Michael-CY Lee <michael-cy.lee@mediatek.com>
Co-developed-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>

